                <fr:title text="What a Verified zkVM Would Mean">What a Verified zkVM Would Mean</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>
    The statement at the top of the whole effort, written out honestly: which theorems compose, and which links in the chain are assumptions rather than proofs. It is the claim the whole effort will be judged on, and its general form is <fr:link href="/dhsorens-001K/" title="Proof Assistants and the Issue of Incorrect Specification" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-001K/" display-uri="dhsorens-001K" type="local">the issue of incorrect specification</fr:link>: a machine-checked proof is only ever as good as the statement it proves.
</html:p>
                <html:p>
    Questions this page should answer:
    <html:ul><html:li>The chain: ISA specification, constraint system, arithmetisation soundness, IOP soundness, commitment security, <fr:link href="/dhsorens-002G/" title="Fiat–Shamir and the Random Oracle Model" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-002G/" display-uri="dhsorens-002G" type="local">Fiat–Shamir</fr:link>, recursion, extracted implementation.</html:li>
        <html:li>Which links are proved today, which are stated, and which are not formalised at all.</html:li>
        <html:li>The irreducible assumptions: <fr:link href="/dhsorens-004D/" title="Hash Functions in Bitcoin and Ethereum" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-004D/" display-uri="dhsorens-004D" type="local">hash security</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/dhsorens-0038/" title="Soundness Regimes and the Proximity-Gap Conjectures" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-0038/" display-uri="dhsorens-0038" type="local">conjectured proximity bounds</fr:link>, the compiler, the hardware.</html:li>
        <html:li>Whether "verified" should mean the composed end-to-end theorem, or a set of component theorems with audited seams.</html:li>
        <html:li>The 2027 target the project set, and what would have to be true for it to be met.</html:li></html:ul></html:p>
                <html:p>
    Sources: <fr:link href="https://verified-zkevm.org/" type="external">verified-zkevm.org</fr:link>, <fr:link href="https://github.com/Verified-zkEVM/Overview" type="external">Verified-zkEVM overview</fr:link>.
</html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
